1
00:00:00,740 --> 00:00:02,410
(Amy:)Sheldon, it's a beautiful night.

2
00:00:02,575 --> 00:00:05,075
(Amy:)Why don't you and I
go for a nice walk together?

3
00:00:05,245 --> 00:00:07,745
(Sheldon:)Oh, everything is just
sex with you isn't it?

4
00:00:09,249 --> 00:00:11,729
(Raj:)Sheldon, I think
you might find the support

5
00:00:11,885 --> 00:00:13,265
(Raj:)you're looking for, if you realize

6
00:00:13,419 --> 00:00:15,529
(Raj:)that relationships
are a give and take.

7
00:00:15,688 --> 00:00:16,928
(Raj:)She can only be there for you

8
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:18,870
(Raj:)as much as you are for her.

9
00:00:19,025 --> 00:00:20,665
(Amy:)Thank you, Rajesh.

10
00:00:20,827 --> 00:00:22,937
(Raj:)And, Amy, you need
to be patient with Sheldon,

11
00:00:23,096 --> 00:00:26,096
(Raj:)instead of pressuring him
to accept intimacy on your terms.

12
00:00:27,834 --> 00:00:29,544
(Sheldon:)You should probably go.

13
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:37,682
(Ira Flatow:)I'm Ira Flatow,
and this is Science Friday.

14
00:00:37,844 --> 00:00:39,794
(Ira:)I'd like to welcome back
Dr. Sheldon Cooper,

15
00:00:39,946 --> 00:00:41,896
(Ira:)who thought
he had discovered

16
00:00:42,048 --> 00:00:44,618
(Ira:)a new super-heavy element
only to have it disproved

17
00:00:44,784 --> 00:00:47,094
(Ira:)by my next guest,
Dr. Leonard Hofstadter.

18
00:00:47,253 --> 00:00:48,393
Welcome to Science Friday,
gentlemen.

19
00:00:48,521 --> 00:00:49,691
(Leonard:)-Thanks.
-Thank you.

20
00:00:49,856 --> 00:00:54,366
(Sheldon:)Ira, if I may, I'd like to apologize
for my behavior last week.

21
00:00:54,527 --> 00:00:55,937
(Ira:)It's all right.

22
00:00:56,095 --> 00:01:01,025
(Sheldon:)Now, isn't there something
you'd like to say to me?

